KZ3 patch 1085 (SPU pass 66, diagnostic, opt-in): event trace hook for a per-frame timeline. kz3_wait_acct
gains g_kz3_wtrace (NULL by default): every accounted bracket and note (HLE calls, syscalls, usleeps, label waits,
kernel sleeps, policy-module runs, GCM parks), every job-module change, every flip and every WWS job call (the jm
policy module, image 2, branching from its own code into the job code buffer at LS[0x1320])
is passed to it with host times and the thread name; so are the GCM walker queueing a user command and a
PPU pump delivering it (cellGcmSys.c). A job call ends when control is back at the PM link: in spu_indirect_branch
when the job returned normally, else when the PM drain returns (spu_drain_call_full wraps its old body). Set by port/spu/kz3_frame_trace.c (KZ3_FRAME_TRACE=FROM,TO).
Off: one predictable branch per indirect branch and per accounted bracket. kz3_wacct_base() exposes KZ3_PROF time zero.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): wrapper ours, body start upstream's (SPU_DIRECT init, `spu_depth_guard_check`, outer_ret_pc restore).

